{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["929be0bf-2d70-4510-aaf4-0ed502cb1c2f"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["af69d415-0295-5123-81c3-7f1c72f9effd"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["71d9ab4b-9446-51e6-aff7-75f083df7f82"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"The Test Performed record for GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10 was edited, and it is still active. It records SARS-CoV-2 (COVID-19) RNA [Presence] in Respiratory system specimen by NAA with probe detection [SCTID 166611010000108]. The analyte is SARS-CoV-2 and the specimen is Nasopharyngeal swab [SCTID 258500001]. The targets are the N, E and RdRP genes. The instruments are GeneXpert Infinity-80 INFINITY 48-48, Infinity-48s INFINITY48-16 and Dx GXIV-2. The example UCUM units value is Not applicable.\n\nI could only read the current state of the record, not the previous version. I can't say which field changed."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["578d9e95-90fd-423f-8c0d-a6b407739fd2"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["e7012be2-769c-5045-805b-196a693ca733"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["e3417d0c-fe97-5a7e-9e13-916546a85a4a"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"New Test Performed Pattern semantic on the device concept **GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10**, which sits under Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents. It records the following:\n- **Test performed:** SARS-CoV-2 (COVID-19) RNA [Presence] in Respiratory system specimen by NAA with probe detection [166611010000108].\n- **Analyte:** SARS-CoV-2.\n- **Targets:** the N, E and RdRP genes.\n- **Specimen:** Swab of internal nose [445297001].\n- **Instruments:** GeneXpert Infinity-80 System INFINITY 48-48, GeneXpert Infinity-48s System INFINITY48-16 and GeneXpert Dx System GXIV-2.\n- **Example UCUM units:** Not applicable [385432009]."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["e1afae64-7def-4927-9c3e-7fe32cc94238"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["261d2f9e-1674-51d6-96b3-a045959a1310"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["b9558877-0dd3-5245-b087-0cd9442fc9b8"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Allowed Results Pattern semantic was added for the device concept GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10. It is a child of Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents. The allowed result set is Detected (260373001), Not detected (260415000), Invalid result (455371000124106), Test not done (373121007) and Specimen unsatisfactory for evaluation (125154007).\n\nThe tools resolved the committed UUID to this semantic, and the concept lookup returned GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10. I could not read the pattern definition itself because the pattern tool returned an error. The link to that concept is therefore inferred from the lookup and not confirmed."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["c783c855-f530-460f-b4ac-4a0c7d2954d4"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["71f9928b-9576-5bf0-aa45-d59bf3b850e8"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["8b9e1612-cd71-5eb2-9817-094fd80385f8"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Limit Metrics Pattern entry was added to **GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10**. It records a limit of detection (LoD) of 143.0 IU/mL. The concept sits under *Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents*. It was committed as active by Device Extension Author on the Device Extension Module.\n\nThe identifier you gave resolves to the semantic itself, and the tools return the GeneXpert concept as its referenced component. I could not read the pattern definition directly, so the link to that concept comes from the concept lookup, not from the pattern record."}]}]}}
