{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["94bee556-6dc2-4313-943d-7f0a139bb7e1"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["de9a81ee-35ae-5c96-902a-58ebc741080b"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["2ba172c5-7232-5a53-99ca-2d62e6b35d14"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"The reasoner committed new inferred definitions for 24 components. The sampled ones are Analyte and Target concepts for respiratory-virus assays, for example Influenza A (Analyte), Influenza B (Analyte), Influenza A Matrix protein (M) gene (Target) and RSV B Nucleocapsid protein (N) gene (Target). In every sampled case the inferred axiom is a plain necessary set whose only parent is Analyte or Target. I didn't check the other 16 components, so the pattern may not hold for all of them."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["8061823a-7321-4f93-a043-9c5da037b1ee"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["ca860b8b-0e82-57ec-a8e7-2ca02391abbd"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["4644ded1-4b34-5d67-8a6e-4899b052e121"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Test Performed record is attached to the device concept GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10, which sits under Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents. It defines an Influenza A analyte test on a nasopharyngeal swab, with targets in the M, PB2 and PA genes. It links four LOINC-style influenza NAA tests: respiratory, upper respiratory, A/B/RSV panel and A/B panel. It also lists three GeneXpert instruments (Infinity-80, Infinity-48s and Dx GXIV-2), and its example units are \"Not applicable\"."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["29d1d9a7-311b-497f-983a-37644cf648b8"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["ec9f3855-e0ff-518a-bf62-2770fa3fad00"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["c9d22168-a1ea-58e8-b19e-f88856a02602"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Allowed Results Pattern semantic was added. It lists five permitted results: Detected [260373001], Not detected [260415000], Specimen unsatisfactory for evaluation [125154007], Test not done [373121007] and Invalid result [455371000124106].\n\nThe tools resolved this component UUID to the device concept GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10, a child of Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents. I couldn't confirm which Test Performed record the semantic is attached to."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["d8d002be-5a4e-4784-a35a-62af4093999e"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["b3026af1-e3c1-51e0-bf01-e923cfe1dd46"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["888fc819-7ce9-5d59-a677-b1c1575fc5a0"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Limit Metrics Pattern entry was added to the Influenza A Test Performed record on **GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10**. That record is the nasopharyngeal swab record, which targets the Influenza A M, PB2 and PA genes. The entry gives a limit of detection (LoD) of 0.44, with units set to \"Not applicable\" (SCTID 385432009). The unit is unspecified, so the value can't be read as a concentration. The device's SARS-CoV-2 records, by contrast, carry LoD values in IU/mL."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["7e2fe502-48c4-4699-abfb-613d59f361c8"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["acd70ae5-18b8-588f-b6fd-1ecf56b9bf4d"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["b249ee2c-8c14-56ed-a637-66ab5bf80c34"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A Device Performance Pattern semantic was added to GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10. It's a child of Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents. The record gives a Sensitivity of 99.0 (Percentage unit, SCTID 415067009), with a 95% confidence interval of 96.3 to 99.7."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["5ddf66f2-4b2c-46f4-8eb6-9e8ef73ce1ae"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["544762f5-5240-5a9f-b9a7-4d44a9ac2643"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["9917fa1a-2200-57c9-aae4-151bf14dbd49"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Device Performance Pattern entry was added for GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10. It records Specificity of 99.1 (Percentage unit), with a 95% confidence interval of 98.7 to 99.4. GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10 is a child of Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents.\n\nThe tools resolved this component UUID to GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10 but did not list the entry as attached to it. I am assuming that is the concept it describes."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["a1cd897b-ab9f-417f-bcf5-0b52e6543799"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["9cc4e146-3163-52a1-878e-29295aea3c2d"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["cc069c4c-ba39-59f2-b106-49f9ff74a7f5"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Test Performed record was added for **GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10**, which sits under Multi-Target Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Test Including Sars-Cov-2 And Other Microbial Agents. It lists Influenza A as the analyte and Swab of internal nose [SCTID 445297001] as the specimen. It links four influenza NAA-with-probe-detection LOINC-style test concepts and three GeneXpert instruments: Infinity-80 INFINITY 48-48, Infinity-48s INFINITY48-16 and Dx GXIV-2. The example UCUM units are \"Not applicable\", and the Target field is empty."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["b40dc37a-6a1f-4729-8122-331a769993a0"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["f354e423-4b73-5bab-bc51-bf42ab82a20f"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["68fe8ea1-85a6-5900-b5b8-08b740a424bc"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Allowed Results semantic was added to the Influenza A Test Performed record on GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10 (Xpert Xpress CoV-2/Flu/RSV plus). That record covers the anterior nasal swab specimen (\"Swab of internal nose\" [445297001]). The allowed results are Detected [260373001], Not detected [260415000], Invalid result [455371000124106], Test not done [373121007] and Specimen unsatisfactory for evaluation [125154007]. This is the same five-value set the device's other Test Performed records already carry."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["1a20d565-5c90-48d6-b8de-4f14bf803dc3"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["f8157c50-929f-5804-88ac-ca31ad8e1bf0"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["edf6cbcb-b005-52e5-ba2c-3e6ad3519865"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Limit Metrics record was added: LoD = 0.49, with units \"Not applicable\" [SCTID 385432009]. It sits on the Influenza A Test Performed entry for GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10 (Xpert Xpress CoV-2/Flu/RSV plus). That entry covers the \"Swab of internal nose\" [SCTID 445297001] specimen and has no gene targets listed."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["d150ccc0-6a00-4609-9d42-f654176f1d77"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["6f009649-aee7-5982-a278-92f731229c59"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["dfda91ab-4941-563b-8723-b51950d29699"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Device Performance record was added to the Influenza A Test Performed entry for GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10 (Xpert Xpress CoV-2/Flu/RSV plus). That entry uses the swab of internal nose specimen and has no targets listed. The record gives a Sensitivity of 98.0% (Percentage unit), with a 95% confidence interval of 95.0–99.2.\n\nThe same Test Performed entry also carries a second Device Performance record. That record is blank: its metric is Blank Concept and every value is 0.0, so it looks like an unfilled placeholder."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["4907ef75-2197-4319-b05f-8b5cd695a098"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["50cc2c1a-048e-5ffc-84d9-e86ca8ea7409"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["c6032bc3-7252-5654-a35f-9f8020b81400"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Device Performance record is now on GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10. It reports a specificity of 99.3% (95% CI 99.0–99.6, unit: Percentage unit). It sits on the Influenza A Test Performed entry for the anterior nasal swab specimen (Swab of internal nose, SCTID 445297001), alongside that entry's existing sensitivity (98.0%) and LoD (0.49) records."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["17c68c0d-1bd5-42d0-ba9e-0c99dd3648a6"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["b1c482db-9f99-55b0-8f22-d6f746de6dc8"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["2f28a921-ccf7-5d18-9de8-e220727fbfb3"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A Test Performed Pattern semantic on GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10 was edited and is still active. The diff wasn't available to me, so I can't say which field changed. It currently records:\n- **Analyte:** Influenza A.\n- **Targets:** the M, PB2 and PA genes.\n- **Specimen:** Swab of internal nose (445297001).\n- **Instruments:** GeneXpert Infinity-80 (INFINITY 48-48), Infinity-48s (INFINITY48-16) and Dx (GXIV-2).\n- **Test Performed:** four NAA-with-probe-detection tests, namely 49931010000101, 240031010000103, 616061010000100 and 620841010000103."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["af73df2a-d5d0-404d-b535-4ce948e835bb"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["1a8e1959-888d-536e-b04e-2120e05c35ed"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["87b8d22f-9474-5573-89b9-ff4d472def9c"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Test Performed record was added for the device GeneXpert® XPRS4PLEX-10. It says the device detects Influenza B (analyte) through the test \"Influenza virus B RNA [Presence] in Upper respiratory specimen by NAA with probe detection\" [SCTID 88331010000104].\n\n- **Targets:** the Influenza B Matrix protein (M) gene and the Influenza B non-structural protein (NS) gene.\n- **Specimen:** Nasopharyngeal swab [SCTID 258500001].\n- **Instruments:** GeneXpert Infinity-80 System INFINITY 48-48, GeneXpert Infinity-48s System INFINITY48-16 and GeneXpert Dx System GXIV-2.\n- **Example UCUM units:** Not applicable [SCTID 385432009].\n\nI inferred the device attachment from the concept lookup, since the component UUID is the semantic instance itself."}]}]}}
{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["c6c9e804-d7fe-4aa5-a051-7b8a33c88d48"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["a4f3b69a-704a-50e9-94a3-03ac31644158"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["bd50fa88-24fc-5bf3-aee4-66be3cec33f0"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"Reasoner results transaction (21 components): the sampled components are all SOLOR/IKE metadata concepts (e.g., Author, Module, Path for user, Phenomenon, Target), and for those I checked, the inferred definitions match the stated ones, so the sample shows no visible hierarchy change. The transaction ID alone does not show which relationships changed, so the full set of 21 should be reviewed before this note is finalized."}]}]}}
